{"id": "EUVD-2025-207830", "enisaUuid": "a0c9b00f-4303-3ebe-ade1-10d227167912", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: don't WARN for connections on invalid channels\n\nIt's not clear (to me) how exactly syzbot managed to hit this,\nbut it seems conceivable that e.g. regulatory changed and has\ndisabled a channel between scanning (channel is checked to be\nusable by cfg80211_get_ies_channel_number) and connecting on\nthe channel later.\n\nWith one scenario that isn't covered elsewhere described above,\nthe warning isn't good, replace it with a (more informative)\nerror message.", "datePublished": "2026-02-18T14:21:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:38:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c02b1d244a5d799696ca74d3fba6539c8d76195f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/579cf5939f8f4c4f88c75862d0c573fb13567b74", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/10d3ff7e5812c8d70300f6fa8f524009a06aa7e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/99067b58a408a384d2a45c105eb3dce980a862ce"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c5gg-v573-hv7f", "CVE-2025-71227"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01037f54-5a18-374d-b228-7e0d1d7d67c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19"}, {"id": "064e96d4-0ee7-398b-bdda-1d0e1ef4bf82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.10"}, {"id": "116ffaa4-0cd2-3beb-b6a1-b67d407a2df5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1c2aedc7-a39a-3744-84e9-860d4681324c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2d9d270c15ae0139b54a7e7466d738327e97e03 <99067b58a408a384d2a45c105eb3dce980a862ce"}, {"id": "44d124fb-217a-3304-b416-0cc35b3dc85c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.8"}, {"id": "998c2810-2af9-3c0c-a12b-f21db2649281", "product":